    lessonSlug: "basketball-hockey-and-baseball",
    lessonTitle: "10 · Basketball, hockey and baseball",
    text: "Costa, B. (2026, January 13). *NHL Situation Room 2.0: How Sony Hawk-Eye powers centralized officiating, player safety, the league's next chapter*. Sports Video Group. Retrieved October 26, 2026, from https://www.sportsvideo.org/2026/01/13/nhl-situation-room-2-0-how-sony-hawk-eye-powers-centralized-officiating-player-safety-the-leagues-next-chapter/ Locator: \"From Replay Reviews to a League-Wide Hub\"; \"The Sony Hawk-Eye Backbone\".",
    url: "https://www.sportsvideo.org/2026/01/13/nhl-situation-room-2-0-how-sony-hawk-eye-powers-centralized-officiating-player-safety-the-leagues-next-chapter/",
    excerpt: "A trade report describes the league's Situation Room in Toronto: \"a dedicated operator\" for each game, feeds from \"standardized goal-line, blue-line, and overhead camera positions,\" and video that can go to officials' iPads on the ice (Costa, 2026).",
