    lessonTitle: "1 · What light does on a stage, in a studio and on a set",
    text: "Selden, S., & Sellman, H. D. (1930). *Stage scenery and lighting: A handbook for non-professionals*. F. S. Crofts. https://archive.org/details/bwb_P8-CET-129 Locator: Part Two (Sellman's), p. 209 (PDF p. 241), read from the page image.",
    url: "https://archive.org/details/bwb_P8-CET-129",
    excerpt: "Five functions, 1930. Hunton D. Sellman's half of a 1930 handbook for non-professionals lists what \"specific illumination\" does: \"(a) Creates relief, true form, for actor and setting (makes them plastic, not flat) (b) Enhances the beauty of the setting by means of color, form, and pattern. (c) Carries out the intended…",
